senses.gloss:
roca (Vedic as adj. once; not in Pali; M. roa once in different mg.),
(1) nt., light (or, possibly, adj., shining): sarvabuddhānusāsanīcakrarocaṃ nāma prajñāpāramitāmukhaṃ Gv 〔449.20〕;
(2) m., a kind of flower: Mvy 〔6183〕 = Tib. me tog mdog mdzes, fair-colored flower or rose;
(3) (= Pali Roja 2 in DPPN) n. of an ancient king, in Pali and Mvy son of Mahāsaṃmata; in Mv, acc. to the (corrupt) ms. which contains the word, son of Kalyāṇa and grandson of Mahāsaṃmata: Mvy 〔3553〕; in Mv 〔i.348.8〕 the v.l. of one ms. shows that this name was in the list, tho it is confused with Rava q.v.;
(4) (= Pali Roja 1 in DPPN) n. of a minister of the Mallas in Pāpā: MSV 〔i.282.2 ff.〕 (uncle of Ānanda, but unbelieving; converted by Buddha).
